        {
          "name": "cancel session",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost/growzy/routes/api.php/session/1",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "path": [
                "growzy",
                "routes",
                "api.php",
                "session",
                "1"
              ]
            },
            "description": "## Cancel Session\n\nCancels a previously booked or scheduled session for a user. This endpoint allows clients to programmatically cancel an active session by providing the session's unique identifier.\n\n---\n\n### When to Use\n\nUse this endpoint when a user wants to cancel a session they have already booked. This is typically triggered from a cancellation flow in the client application (e.g., a \"Cancel Session\" button on a booking details page).\n\n---\n\n### Path Variables\n\n| Variable | Type | Required | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `id` | string | ✅ Yes | The unique identifier of the session to be cancelled. |\n\n> **Example:** `/sessions/:id/cancel` \n  \n\n---\n\n### Query Parameters\n\nNo query parameters are required for this endpoint.\n\n---\n\n### Expected Responses\n\n#### ✅ Success — `200 OK`\n\nThe session was successfully cancelled.\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"message\": \"Session cancelled successfully.\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"abc123\",\n  \"status\": \"cancelled\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n#### ❌ Not Found — `404 Not Found`\n\nThe session with the provided ID does not exist.\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"error\": \"Session not found.\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"abc123\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n#### ❌ Conflict — `409 Conflict`\n\nThe session has already been cancelled or cannot be cancelled in its current state.\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"error\": \"Session cannot be cancelled. It may have already been cancelled or completed.\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n#### ❌ Unauthorized — `401 Unauthorized`\n\nThe request is missing or contains an invalid authentication token.\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"error\": \"Unauthorized. Please provide a valid token.\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n---\n\n### Notes\n\n- Ensure the session ID is valid and belongs to the authenticated user before making this request.\n    \n- Once cancelled, the session status cannot be reverted. Use the reschedule endpoint if the user wants to change the session time instead of cancelling it."
          },
          "response": []
        },
